{%- comment -%}
  Card title on two lines: the name, then the product type.

    WALTERIN PRAGUE          TAROT OF CONSCIOUSNESS      WALTERIN PRAGUE
    COMIC BOOK               A GRAPHIC JOURNEY           STICKER SET

  The product title in Shopify is never changed — this only decides where the
  card breaks it. Order of preference:

  1. `walterin.card_line_2` on the product. It holds the SECOND line only, and
     it is a translated metafield, so Slovak can say something different from
     English — or say nothing, and the card falls back to one line. This is the
     field to fill in for a new product, and the only one that handles a title
     whose two halves are not separated by punctuation
     ("Walterin Prague Sticker Set"), or whose word order changes between
     languages ("Sada nálepiek Walterin Praha").

  2. Failing that, the title is split on its own punctuation — a colon or a
     dash. "Walterin Vienna – Comic Book" therefore works on the day it is
     created, with no metafield at all.

  3. Failing that, one line. Never a guess.

  Line one is the title with line two taken off the end, then any leftover
  separator. The separator is dropped rather than shown: on two lines the line
  break already does the work a dash or colon was doing, and "WALTERIN PRAGUE –"
  hanging at the end of a line reads like something went wrong.

  Accepts: card_product (required), link_class, link_attrs
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign t = card_product.title | strip
  assign line_1 = t
  assign line_2 = ''

  assign explicit = card_product.metafields.walterin.card_line_2.value | default: '' | strip

  if explicit != blank
    assign line_2 = explicit
    assign head = t | split: line_2 | first | strip
    assign rest = t | split: line_2 | last | strip
    if head != blank and head != t
      comment
        The usual shape: the title ends with line two. "Walterin Prague Sticker
        Set" minus "Sticker Set" leaves the name.
      endcomment
      assign line_1 = head
    elsif head == blank and rest != blank and rest != t
      comment
        Slovak puts the type first: "Sada nálepiek Walterin Praha". Line two is
        at the FRONT, so the name is whatever follows it, and the card still
        reads name over type.
      endcomment
      assign line_1 = rest
    endif
  elsif t contains ': '
    comment
      A colon belongs to the first line — it is part of the title, not a joint
      between two halves, so it stays put: "Tarot of Consciousness:".
    endcomment
    assign parts = t | split: ': '
    assign line_1 = parts | first | strip | append: ':'
    assign line_2 = parts | last | strip
  else
    comment
      A dash is only a connector, so it goes: on two lines the break already
      does its job and a dash left hanging reads like a mistake.
    endcomment
    assign dashes = ' – | — | - '
    assign dash_list = dashes | split: '|'
    for sep in dash_list
      if line_2 == blank and t contains sep
        assign parts = t | split: sep
        assign line_1 = parts | first | strip
        assign line_2 = parts | last | strip
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    A dash left dangling at the end of line one goes, whichever branch produced
    it. A colon never does.
  endcomment
  assign last_ch = line_1 | slice: -1, 1
  if last_ch == '–' or last_ch == '—' or last_ch == '-'
    assign line_1 = line_1 | replace_last: last_ch, '' | strip
  endif

  if line_1 == blank
    assign line_1 = t
    assign line_2 = ''
  endif
-%}

<a
  href="{{ card_product.url }}"
  class="{{ link_class | default: 'full-unstyled-link' }}"
  {{ link_attrs }}
>
  <span class="wui-card-title__name">{{ line_1 | escape }}</span>
  {%- if line_2 != blank -%}
    <span class="wui-card-title__type">{{ line_2 | escape }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</a>
